# admin-auth credential (ADMIN_PORTAL_PLAN §3) — EXAMPLE. One `user:hash` line.
#
# The real file `htpasswd` is gitignored. The first-boot flow materialises it
# from ADMIN_AUTH_USER and ADMIN_AUTH_HASH in .env, the same way
# oauth2-proxy/authenticated-emails.txt is written from its .env knob.
#
# The hash is bcrypt from `caddy hash-password`: oauth2-proxy reads the same
# `$2a$` format Caddy's basic_auth did, which is why the password the Owner
# already used for actual.<domain> carries over unchanged (store key
# ActualBasicAuthHash). In .env every `$` is doubled; in THIS file it is not —
# compose interpolates .env, nothing interpolates this.
#
# It is a single-file bind mount: on a running box EDIT IT IN PLACE
# (`cat new > htpasswd`). Replacing the inode leaves the container reading the
# old file. oauth2-proxy re-reads it on change; no restart needed.
#
# The container runs as uid 65532, so the file must be readable by that uid.
#
# Placeholder only — never a real hash here:
admin:REPLACE_WITH_caddy_hash-password_OUTPUT
